    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1543">

                <pb facs="1248" n="1132" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1132"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.48/22</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 76.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 10, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose a copy of a
                        letter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1543-f1"/> from the French consular
                    representative in Nicaragua requesting me to forward to Granada food supplies
                    furnished by him to certain of his nationals who have had to endure the
                    hardships imposed on foreigners and natives alike by Mena’s lawless bands. The
                    Legation was of course glad to be able to comply with the request.</p>
                <p>I am also transmitting copies of letters<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1543-f2"/>
                    received from Americans and other residents of Granada, briefly describing
                    conditions which recently prevailed in that city under the Mena régime.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George T. Weitzel.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
